      "id": "534",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 534,
        "relationship_type": "related",
        "body": "そういう (and its variants こういう, ああいう, どういう) and そんな・こんな・あんな・どんな both modify nouns to mean 'that sort of,' 'this sort of,' etc. While often similar in meaning, そういう tends to be a bit more formal or polite. In contrast, depending on context そんな can be used with a negative or dismissive tone, which is not true of そういう.",
        "first_relatable": {
