    {
      "id": "1263",
      "type": "related_content",
      "attributes": {
        "id": 1263,
        "relationship_type": "misc",
        "body": "そんな・こんな・あんな・どんな are used before nouns and mean 'that/this/what kind of' or 'something like (A)'. This is a common and fairly casual pattern in everyday speech. いかなる is similar to どんな, but with a much more formal or literary tone. For example, いかなることがあっても and どんなことがあっても both mean 'no matter what happens', but the いかなる version sounds much more formal.",
        "first_relatable": {
